{"assertions":[{"answerability":"answerable","basis":"Souvay's \"Isaias\" in the Catholic Encyclopedia places the prophetical ministry \"from the closing year of Ozias, King of Juda,\" which it gives as the year of that prince's death, \"740 B.C.\", and holds that \"since no prophecies appear to be later than 701 B.C. , it is doubtful if Isaias saw the reign of Manasses at all.\" Of the collection the article says it \"might still possibly be attributed to the last years of the Prophet's life or shortly afterwards.\"","basis_class":"traditional-catholic","date":"740 B.C.-701 B.C.","derived":false,"disposition":"preferred","inherited":true,"label":"from the closing year of Ozias, King of Juda (740 B.C.); no prophecies appear to be later than 701 B.C.","note":"The two years date the PROPHET'S MINISTRY, which is the period the book's prophecies come from; the article assigns no year to the writing or final assembly of the collection and is expressly guarded about it — \"The foregoing analysis does not enable us to assert indubitably that this first collection as such is the work of Isaias.\" 740 is attached by the article to the death of Ozias while reporting Jerome's view of chapter vi, and 701 is the article's own inference (\"appear to be\"). The traditional position on AUTHORSHIP carries no year and is therefore not a second claim: the Pontifical Biblical Commission, 28 June 1908, decided that \"There are no solid arguments to the fore, even taken cumulatively, to prove that the book of Isaias is to be attributed not to Isaias himself alone, but to two or rather to many authors\". The article concedes that the author of xl-lxvi \"does speak from the point of view of the Babylonian Captivity.\"","precision":"range","profile":"catholic-traditional-v1","relation":"composition","reporting_exception":null,"scope":"Is","sources":["artifact.catholic-encyclopedia.volume-8.new-york-1910.newadvent-08179b-d4ee13fd"],"subject":"composition.book-of-isaias","title":"The Book of Isaias"}],"chronology_status":"composition-only","locus":"Is.55.7","reason":"","requested_profile":"catholic-comprehensive-v1","resolved_profiles":{"composition":"catholic-traditional-v1"},"status":"ok","v":1}
